kanfei (0.1.0~beta68) unstable; urgency=medium

  * History (backend): 5-minute bucket labels now land on the actual
    bucket start.  The ``time_label`` column in the 5m aggregate
    query used ``strftime`` on the raw timestamp of an arbitrary row
    inside each bucket — so two sensors sampled at different phases
    inside the same 5-minute window returned different labels for
    that window.  Highcharts placed the series at slightly different
    x positions and dragging the cursor across the chart caught
    whichever tooltip was nearest — visible as cross-series
    misalignment.  Compute the label from ``bucket * 300`` unixepoch
    so it's identity-independent.  Regression test added:
    ``test_5m_labels_land_on_bucket_starts`` asserts every returned
    label ends ``:00Z`` and its minute is a multiple of five.

