kanfei (0.1.0~beta38) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixes GET /api/history?resolution=5m so it actually returns 5-min
    buckets rather than raw rows.  SQLAlchemy 2.0 emits float division
    for the Python `/` operator on numeric columns as a portability
    hedge; on SQLite that puts every unix-timestamp second into its
    own bucket, so the GROUP BY silently didn't collapse and 24 h
    returned ~8k rows instead of ~288.  Forced SQL integer division
    with .op("/"); charts requesting "5m" now get true 5-min averages
    with per-bucket min/max, the sample-count kicker matches reality,
    and the payload is 27x smaller.  Regression test suite in
    test_history_aggregate.py fails if this ever slips again.

  * Fixes the wind rose (Everyday, Agriculture drift-risk, Weather
    Nerd) so it draws from live data instead of a fixed 16-petal
    placeholder that had been shipping unchanged since the tile
    landed.  A new adapter fetch pulls wind_direction at raw
    resolution over the last 4 h (matching the "Wind rose · 4 h"
    kicker), buckets into 16 22.5-degree wedges centred on N/E/S/W,
    normalises to a max of 1.0, and passes the weights to the tiles.
    localStorage-hydrated so the rose comes back on refresh.

