kanfei (0.1.0~beta31) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Adds a public-facing droplet mode.  Kanfei can now run on a second
    machine — a small cloud droplet, typically — that displays live
    weather data pushed from a private station without exposing any
    write surface.  The droplet runs the exact same package as the
    private station; the only difference is a driver selection at
    setup time.  Every write endpoint returns 403 except two
    bearer-authenticated ingest paths that accept snapshot pushes from
    the private station.  Guests browse the dashboard, live tiles, and
    read-only Settings; nothing they do can change state or reach the
    private station's hardware.  Full operator documentation lives at
    docs/public-droplet.md, with a reference nginx recipe at
    reference/nginx-public-droplet.conf.example that terminates TLS
    and locks the ingest paths to the private station's outbound IP.

  * Adds a Public Droplet Relay section to the Station settings tab on
    the private station side.  Toggle it on, paste the droplet's URL
    and the shared bearer secret you set on the droplet, and Save.
    The relay task in kanfei-logger picks up the change on the next
    poll cycle — no restart — and starts pushing every sensor snapshot
    to the droplet's ingest endpoint alongside the existing Weather
    Underground and CWOP uploads.  The panel surfaces a red banner
    with the last push failure so an operator sees a stalled relay
    without having to tail the systemd journal.

