kanfei (0.1.0~beta30) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Adds three new rows to the Solar & UV tile.  The first is the
    console's own evapotranspiration totals — a per-day, per-month, and
    per-year running measure of how much water the atmosphere is pulling
    out of your ground and plants.  Davis stations compute it from
    solar radiation, temperature, humidity, and wind, and the values
    were already coming off the wire on every poll; this surfaces them
    on the tile in your rain units (inches or millimetres).  The second
    is a cumulative daily solar energy total — the running integral of
    solar radiation since local midnight, in your choice of MJ per
    square metre, kWh per square metre, or Wh per square metre (chosen
    in Settings > Units > Solar Energy).  Useful if you are tracking
    grid-tie solar, backyard panels, or clear-sky performance day to
    day.  The third is a UV Index warning band under the current UV
    reading — Low, Moderate, High, Very High, or Extreme, per the
    World Health Organisation's Global Solar UV Index bands.

  * Adds two new rows to the Station Status panel showing transmitter
    and console battery health.  Vantage consoles already report these
    on every poll — a bitmask of which sensor transmitters are running
    low on their coin cell, and the raw voltage of the console's own
    supercapacitor-plus-coin-cell backup — but nothing on the dashboard
    was reading them, so a slowly-dying transmitter would silently drop
    dashes into your daily records until you noticed at the console.
    The panel now shows "OK" (in green) when all transmitters are
    happy, "Low: TX1, TX3" (in red) when any are flagged, and the
    console voltage in volts (in yellow below four volts, where the
    coin cell backup is likely spent).  Rows hide entirely on stations
    that don't report battery status.

  * The Astronomy panel now prefers the console's own sunrise and
    sunset times over the server's own astronomical computation when
    the console reports them.  Davis stations compute sunrise and
    sunset from the coordinates you configured on the console itself
    and display them on the LCD; the response shape gains
    sunrise_source and sunset_source markers so a consumer can tell
    which displayed value came from where.  Solar
    noon and twilight ranges continue to come from the astronomical
    computation, since the console doesn't report those.

  * Adds an ET Today, ET This Month, and ET This Year time-series to
    the History page — each chartable across any of the standard
    presets like the temperature and rain series already there.  The
    ET values now live in dedicated database columns (a one-time
    migration copies existing history from the vendor-extras blob into
    the new columns on first startup), so charting them is direct and
    fast rather than requiring a JSON extraction on every query.

  * Adds a Daily Solar Energy series to the History page, rendered as
    a column chart with one bar per calendar day.  The server
    integrates each day's solar radiation samples into a single energy
    total, in the operator's chosen solar-energy unit.  The bar for
    today grows through the day; days with no data show as gaps.
    Useful for comparing sunny days across weeks or verifying the
    output curve of a panel array.

