kanfei (0.1.0~beta29) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Station Clock row on the Station Status panel now ticks every
    second between polls instead of freezing for the five-minute gap
    between backend refreshes.  The console's clock stays visible and
    live, which stops the false-alarm impulse to click "Sync" when the
    console is actually in fine shape — the display was stale, not the
    clock.  The tick is pure client-side extrapolation from the last
    polled snapshot, so no additional serial traffic is added: real
    console drift (a few seconds per week on a crystal oscillator)
    still shows up as a small persistent offset until the next
    auto-sync.  The station's own wall-clock components are advanced
    forward without any timezone conversion, so the display matches
    what your console face shows regardless of where your browser is.

  * The midnight rain rollover — the once-a-day task that captures
    yesterday's rain total and clears the daily counter for the new
    day — now works on every driver, not just Davis.  Until this
    release, non-Davis stations (Tempest, and any future TCP/HTTP
    drivers) silently skipped the rollover; their "Yesterday" tile
    stayed frozen forever on whatever value it happened to hold when
    the station was first added.  Kanfei now reads the day's terminal
    total from its own database (which every driver's polling path
    writes to) and persists it as yesterday, which is the shared
    contract every driver already participates in.  Davis stations
    additionally clear their hardware register, same as before —
    that half is unchanged, including the "clear must succeed before
    yesterday is committed" safeguard added earlier.

  * Removes a legacy state-file migration branch that seeded the
    poller's cached daily rain value using a hardcoded conversion
    that was only correct at the default rain calibration.  The
    branch was already effectively unreachable — the state file is
    rewritten on every clean shutdown, so anyone who had restarted
    Kanfei since the format switched had long since moved to the
    new key.  The removal is a defensive cleanup: nobody with a
    non-default rain calibration will get a subtly-wrong seed on
    their first post-restore poll cycle.

