kanfei (0.1.0~beta28) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Shows the console's Davis product SKU on the Station Status panel.
    The console reports its 4-digit product number in response to an
    undocumented `IDENT` query, and the value is stable per hardware
    revision — a Vue Console shows 6351, a Vue Wireless with WeatherLink
    IP shows 6350, and so on.  Reading it once at connect lets Kanfei
    tell you which specific unit is talking, useful when you have
    multiple consoles on the bench or when you are troubleshooting
    whether the hardware in front of you is the model whose firmware
    quirks a doc is describing.  Populated on Vue and Vantage Pro2;
    blank on stations that predate the command or on non-Davis drivers.

  * Adds an RX Diagnostics tile to the About page for Davis Vue and
    Vantage Pro2 consoles.  Bundles two reads behind one refresh:
    reception counters (packets received/missed, longest unbroken run,
    resyncs, CRC errors, derived reception rate) so you can see whether
    your sensors are being heard, and radio state (band, channel, radio
    domain, crystal calibration, console temperature) so you can confirm
    the console is listening where you expect it to.  Manual refresh
    only — each read holds the console's serial lock briefly, so a
    polling tile would starve the logger.  The tile hides itself
    entirely on non-Vantage stations and for non-admin users.

  * Adds a wire-audit script (`scripts/vantage_wire_audit.py`) that
    records the console's response to every documented Davis serial
    command plus a full 4 KB EEPROM dump.  Read-only, no writes.  This
    is the script that produced the fw 4.33 audit report captured in
    `reference/vantage_fw433_wire_audit.md` — useful when you suspect
    a firmware difference is behind a reception or calibration quirk.

  * Documentation: full wire-audit report for Vantage Vue console
    firmware 4.33 (`reference/vantage_fw433_wire_audit.md`).  Diffs
    the fw 4.33 wire behaviour against the Davis Serial Communication
    Reference and the widely-deployed fw 2.12, calls out three
    departures and five undocumented but universal commands, and
    records what NOT to touch (the bare `RESET` command puts a Vue into
    a setup-wizard-required state on the LCD).

