kanfei (0.1.0~beta27) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Adds a multi-station cross-check to the barometer calibration reference.
    Kanfei used to ask nearby airport reports for their altimeter setting and
    show you the nearest one; a single bad METAR could pin your console's
    persistent offset to a wrong number without any second opinion.  The
    panel now aggregates the reports it fetched: it takes the median of each
    station's observations from the last two hours, then takes the median of
    those medians against the median of your console's last fifteen minutes
    of readings.  Two safeguards decide whether to recommend a write.  It
    refuses when only one station voted, because one reference cannot
    cross-check itself.  It also refuses when the stations disagree by more
    than 0.4 hPa, because it cannot then tell which of them has drifted; it
    shows the per-station values so you can see why it held.  When both
    safeguards pass, it displays how closely the stations agree, the median
    they arrived at, and the recommended offset for your console.

  * Adds a panel for the console's yearly-rain-reset month.  Every Davis
    Vantage console keeps a setting that says which month the yearly rain
    total drops back to zero.  The factory default is January, which is fine
    almost everywhere.  West-coast US installs and anyone tracking a
    hydrological "water year" typically want July, so a winter storm season
    is not split across two yearly totals.  Reading and changing this used
    to require walking to the console.  Kanfei now shows it and can change
    it, and re-reads the register after the write so a change that did not
    take is reported as such rather than as success.

  * Shows the console's firmware version and build date in the Station
    Status panel.  Both come from what your console reported when Kanfei
    first connected, so there is no additional serial traffic.  The row is
    hidden when the station does not report a firmware version, so nothing
    empty appears on legacy stations.

  * Solar radiation is now included in Kanfei's CWOP uploads.  The APRS
    weather format has a standard field for it (Lxxx for 0-999 W/m², lxxx
    for 1000-1999), and Kanfei was silent on it before; readings will now
    show alongside the temperature and pressure on findU and MADIS for any
    station with a solar sensor.  UV is not sent because the APRS format has
    no field for it, and remains Weather Underground only.

  * Adds solar radiation and UV to the per-channel mute list.  Every other
    sensor already had a Settings toggle that drops it from every outbound
    upload when the sensor is misbehaving; solar and UV now do too.  Muting
    one does not affect the other, because they are on physically separate
    channels on the Vantage ISS.

  * Fix: on a Vantage console the on-connect clock sync used to be skipped,
    so the first sync had to wait for the frontend to poll station status
    (about five minutes after reconnect).  Vantage now gets its clock synced
    at connect, immediately.  The five-second-drift check on every panel
    load continues to run for both drivers.

  * Fix: a stale 401 that arrived after a successful login could bounce the
    freshly authenticated user back to the login page.  The frontend
    now takes note of whether a request was made while logged in when it
    was sent, so a response that answers a request made while logged out
    can no longer eject a user who has since logged in.

  * Adds the Vantage Vue Console Manual and the Vantage Pro2 sensor
    installation manual to the reference documents shipped with the source
    tree, alongside the serial protocol reference that was already there.
    These are the authoritative sources for what settings the console
    exposes to the user and how the outdoor hardware is meant to be
    installed.  Not visible in the product itself.

 -- Chris Nighswonger <dev@veritassuperaitsolutions.com>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 21:33:54 +0000

kanfei (0.1.0~beta26) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Adds a per-sensor calibration panel for Vantage consoles, covering the
    inside and outside temperature and humidity offsets your console keeps
    in its own memory.  These are separate from barometer calibration and
    work differently: each is a small correction applied to one sensor.
    Temperature offsets are held in tenths of a degree, so the panel shows
    and accepts whole degrees to the tenth rather than the raw number —
    entering 2.5 means two and a half degrees, not twenty-five.

  * Adds a panel showing the console's own record highs and lows for the
    day, month and year, beside the ones Kanfei has calculated.  The console
    samples continuously while Kanfei reads it every ten seconds, so the
    console may have caught a gust or a spike that fell between readings.
    Where the two disagree, the difference is a measure of what our sampling
    missed.  Sensors your station does not have are shown as blank rather
    than as a reading of zero.

  * Adds the ability to send Kanfei's configured location to a Vantage
    console, which uses it for its own sunrise and sunset times and for
    part of its pressure correction.  The console stores latitude and
    longitude only to a tenth of a degree — roughly seven miles — so the
    panel compares the two at that resolution rather than exactly, and
    reports what the console actually holds after rounding rather than what
    was sent.  The push is one-directional: Kanfei's location is the more
    precise of the two, so it is never overwritten by the console's copy.

  * Adds two console maintenance operations for Vantage stations, each
    behind a confirmation that first states what it will cost.  Setting the
    year's rain total overwrites what the console has counted; before doing
    so, Kanfei shows the console's current total beside the last one it
    recorded and how long ago that was, so rain that fell since the last
    reading is visible before it is discarded.  Clearing the archive erases
    records the console has not yet handed over; Kanfei shows how many it
    already holds first.  Both refuse to run without explicit confirmation.

  * Fix: the elevation shown in the barometer calibration panel and the one
    in the Location card below it could disagree by a foot or two and say
    nothing about it.  Any difference is now shown, stated both in feet and
    as the pressure error it causes, so a discrepancy too small to matter is
    visible as such rather than hidden.

  * Fix: your configured elevation was being rounded to whole feet when it
    was first looked up, which lost precision that the sunrise and sunset
    calculations and the published weather data both use.  The stored value
    now keeps its accuracy, and is rounded only when sent to a console,
    which accepts whole feet.

  * Adds a barometer calibration tool for Davis Vantage stations, reachable
    from Settings.  It shows what your console currently reads, lists nearby
    airport weather reports with how far away and how recent each one is,
    and shows the difference between them.  Applying a calibration tells the
    console what the pressure should be right now, and it works out its own
    correction.  A separate button clears the correction and returns the
    console to its uncalibrated reading.  Airport reports are used because
    they measure pressure the same way a Vantage displays it, so the two
    figures are directly comparable.  Reports more than half an hour old are
    flagged, and more than an hour old will not be applied without
    confirmation — the console calibrates against the pressure at the moment
    you press the button, so an old reading would bake in whatever the
    weather has done since.  This tool is offered only on Vantage consoles;
    the older Weather Monitor and Wizard adjust their barometer by a
    different mechanism that works in the opposite direction.

  * Fix: a calibration that the console rejected reported "calibration
    unchanged", which was not true.  Testing against a console found that a
    rejected command still applies the elevation you sent, even though the
    pressure is refused.  Failed calibrations now report what the station
    actually reads afterwards instead of claiming nothing happened.

  * Fix: applying a barometer calibration could report a failure after
    thirty seconds while having actually succeeded.  Reading the console's
    calibration took fifteen seconds, because the console signals the end of
    its reply by falling silent and Kanfei waited the full serial timeout
    three times over to be sure.  A calibration now completes in under seven
    seconds and reports its result correctly.

  * Adds console reception diagnostics for Vantage stations: how many sensor
    transmissions the console has received, missed, or had to correct since
    midnight.  These are the numbers that show a transmitter going weak
    before the data starts looking strange.

  * The version number now appears in the page footer and on the About page,
    and is recorded correctly in backups and in the public weather data.
    Previously every release reported itself as 0.1.0 regardless of which
    one it was, so a backup could not say which version produced it.

