kanfei (0.1.0~beta23) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: wind gust is now the station's real gust.  On Davis Vantage
    stations the LOOP2 packet — which carries the console's own 10-minute
    gust, the 2- and 10-minute average wind, THSW index, and 15-minute and
    hourly rain — was requested incorrectly and never once arrived.  The
    console sent the first packet and stopped; the second read timed out
    and was discarded without a word, so the failure was invisible for the
    life of the install.  On the development station that was 714,779
    readings without a single LOOP2 value.  Because the published gust
    falls back to the largest wind reading since midnight when no real
    gust is available, dashboards, Weather Underground and CWOP/APRS have
    been receiving the daily maximum in place of a gust.  Expect your
    reported gust to change after upgrading — the console samples the
    anemometer far faster than the polling interval, so the old value
    systematically under-reported.  A missing LOOP2 packet is now logged
    rather than silently dropped.

  * Fix: an absent wind sensor no longer publishes a 255 mph gust.  When a
    Vantage transmitter drops out, the console reports the maximum byte
    value in the wind-speed field to mean "no reading".  That sentinel was
    stored as a real 255 mph measurement, and because the daily maximum
    outlives the outage that produced it, every subsequent upload carried
    the bad gust for the rest of the day — including to CWOP/APRS, where it
    was publicly visible long after the sensor recovered.  Sentinel values
    are now rejected on arrival, and the daily high/low figures are checked
    against each sensor's valid range before publication, a check that
    charts and CSV exports already applied but the published path did not.

  * Fix: sunrise and sunset times on Vantage stations.  Both were read from
    the wrong offsets in the LOOP packet, landing in the console's alarm
    block rather than the sun times, so the displayed values were unrelated
    to actual sunrise and sunset.  Transmitter battery status and console
    battery voltage are now read correctly as well, and a console reporting
    no clock is treated as unknown instead of midnight.

  * Adds full Davis Vantage command support, completing the driver: daily,
    monthly and yearly high/low retrieval; barometer calibration readout;
    EEPROM dump; receiver/transmitter status; clearing of stored highs and
    lows; setting yearly rain and evapotranspiration totals; full archive
    download; and setting station latitude and longitude over the wire.
    Several of these correct errors in Davis's own published documentation,
    each verified against real hardware; the discrepancies are catalogued in
    the repository for future reference.

  * Fix: station settings and clock controls are now offered based on what
    the connected station can actually do, rather than on its driver type.
    Vantage stations were shown controls that did nothing, and hidden from
    controls they supported.

 -- Chris Nighswonger <dev@veritassuperaitsolutions.com>  Sun, 02 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +0000

kanfei (0.1.0~beta22) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: upload credentials no longer reach the systemd journal.  The
    logger daemon wrote your Weather Underground password to the journal in
    plaintext on every upload — roughly every 21 seconds, for as long as
    journal retention held.  The HTTP client logs full request URLs, and the
    PWS upload protocol carries credentials as query-string parameters; the
    web service suppressed that logging but the logger daemon, a separate
    entrypoint, never did.  Logging setup now lives in one shared place that
    every entrypoint uses, and a redaction filter strips credential values
    from any log line that reaches a handler, so a future component cannot
    reopen the hole.  CWOP/APRS and the nowcast client were audited and are
    unaffected.  ACTION REQUIRED: treat any Weather Underground password
    used with an earlier release as disclosed and rotate it AFTER upgrading
    — rotating first simply leaks the new value the same way — and consider
    purging existing journal entries.  Closes #206.

  * Fix: Davis Vantage archive download now works.  Downloading historical
    records from a Vantage Pro, Pro2 or Vue silently returned nothing on
    every attempt, so archive backfill has never functioned for those
    stations; because the failure looked like "no new records" rather than
    an error, nothing ever reported it.  Three separate defects were
    involved: the response header was read as 4 bytes instead of 6, the
    console was never sent the acknowledgement it waits for before
    transmitting each page, and the page parser ignored the leading
    sequence byte — which shifted every field by one and decoded
    timestamps in the year 2126 and temperatures of -487°F.  A corrupt
    page now retries in place rather than desynchronising the stream, and
    a total protocol failure raises instead of being indistinguishable
    from an empty archive.  Verified against real hardware: 0 records
    before, 41 after.  Closes #207.

  * Fix: Vantage temperature and humidity calibration offsets now take
    effect.  Writing an offset appeared to succeed — the value stored and
    read back correctly — but the reading never changed, because the
    console only applies a new calibration after being sent the documented
    CALED/CALFIX sequence.  The outside-humidity offset was also written to
    the wrong address, one byte off, where it adjusted a nonexistent extra
    sensor instead.  Closes #209.

  * Fix: a Vantage Vue no longer reports itself as a Vantage Pro2, and no
    longer appears as "Weather Wizard III" on the dashboard and public API.
    The model code was read from the wrong memory area, and separately,
    readings from any non-legacy station were stored with a station-type
    value that happened to be a valid code for a different, much older
    Davis model.  Closes #208, #215.

  * New: the UI font size is adjustable from the custom theme editor.  A
    slider between 0.85x and 1.75x scales text throughout the interface,
    including gauge labels, and is saved with your custom theme.  Existing
    themes are unaffected and continue to render exactly as before.

  * New: Vantage stations can set the archive interval and clear archive
    memory from the driver, matching capability the legacy Davis driver has
    always had.  Note that, contrary to Davis's own documentation, setting
    the interval does NOT clear existing records — the archive will hold a
    mix of old and new intervals until explicitly cleared.

  * Adds the Davis Vantage Serial Communication Reference to the repository.
    Its absence was the direct cause of the address-map errors behind
    several of the fixes above.

  * Dependency and CI updates: React 19.2.8, react-router 7.18, Vite 8.1,
    three.js 0.185.1, typescript-eslint 8.62, and current GitHub Actions.

 -- Chris Nighswonger <dev@veritassuperaitsolutions.com>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 19:00:30 +0000

kanfei (0.1.0~beta21) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the backup-restore endpoint now writes the restored database
    to the path your live install actually reads from, regardless of
    what the source backup's manifest called its database file.
    Previously, restoring a backup taken on an install whose database
    was named anything other than "kanfei.db" (notably the legacy
    "weather.db" naming used by Windows dev-checkout installs) would
    silently write to that source-named path instead of the live
    "kanfei.db", leaving the live install untouched and the user's
    data orphaned on disk — with a success message and no warning.
    This release derives the destination from KANFEI_DB_PATH directly
    and emits an INFO log line whenever the source and target
    filenames differ so the rename is visible.  The CLI restore
    command (python station.py restore) also picks up the same fix,
    including correct behaviour when restoring against a not-yet-
    existent destination on a fresh install.  Closes #179.

 -- Chris Nighswonger <dev@veritassuperaitsolutions.com>  Wed, 27 May 2026 20:32:46 +0000

kanfei (0.1.0~beta20) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the 3D pressure-field view now renders with the intended smooth
    cubic-interpolated surface on every .deb install.  Since the 3D view
    first shipped, the backend's smooth-surface code path required scipy,
    but scipy was declared only in an optional "nexrad" dependency group
    that the .deb's postinst doesn't install — so every .deb-installed
    kanfei silently fell back to plain inverse-distance-weighting and the
    rendered surface was visibly bumpier than designed.  This release
    moves scipy into the main runtime dependencies; the postinst's
    existing pip-install step picks it up on first install or upgrade.
    Adds ~30MB to the venv install size.  Closes #177.

 -- Chris Nighswonger <dev@veritassuperaitsolutions.com>  Wed, 27 May 2026 00:34:58 +0000

kanfei (0.1.0~beta19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: archive-period readings on legacy Davis stations (Weather Monitor /
    Wizard / Perception / GroWeather / Energy / Health) are correct for the
    first time.  A memory-map register declaration shipped at the wrong link
    bank since v0.1.0, so every read of the station's archive-period register
    returned a different garbage byte from an unrelated sensor field.  Effects
    observed by users: the history chart's time-bin resolution looked off
    because each archive row was tagged with a bogus interval; the
    station-config "archive period" value in Settings could show an impossible
    value like 68 or 102 minutes; and the daemon could push that bogus value
    back to the station's hardware register on every restart.  This release
    fixes the register address, validates every read and write against the
    Davis-legal set {1, 5, 10, 15, 30, 60, 120}, and ships a one-shot
    self-heal that runs on the first connect after upgrade: the daemon
    rewrites the canonical archive-period to the correct freshly-read value
    AND fixes every historical archive_records row that was tagged with a
    bogus interval — both in a single connect, no manual steps.  Vantage Pro
    and Vantage Pro 2 users are unaffected by this bug; they use a separate
    driver path that was never wrong.  Closes #174.

 -- Chris Nighswonger <dev@veritassuperaitsolutions.com>  Tue, 26 May 2026 23:03:50 +0000

kanfei (0.1.0~beta18) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: "Yesterday" rain tile is no longer permanently stuck at 0.  The
    midnight rollover task that captures the prior day's rain total has
    been silently dead on every kanfei install since v0.1.0 due to a
    dangling-attribute bug in the daemon loop — the task raised
    AttributeError on first iteration and asyncio swallowed it.  This
    release re-enables the rollover.  Davis stations with non-default
    rain_cal (e.g. the rain_cal=254 workaround from beta14) will also
    record the correct yesterday value now: the conversion goes through
    the same calibration-aware helper added in beta14.  The hardware
    clear runs before the persist commits, so a failed hardware clear
    leaves yesterday untouched and the daemon retries at the next
    midnight rather than double-counting.  Non-Davis drivers (Tempest,
    Ambient, etc.) still don't get yesterday rollover — tracked
    separately — but no longer emit a misleading "station not
    connected" warning every midnight.  Closes #170.

