kanfei (0.1.0~beta16) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: per-channel CWOP/APRS mute.  Operators can now take an individual
    sensor out of CWOP service (e.g. while it's under repair or known to
    be miscalibrated) without dropping the rest of the station from the
    public feed and without polluting CWOP with bad readings.  Nine
    channels are individually toggleable in Settings → CWOP — Sensor
    Reporting (outdoor temperature, outdoor humidity, wind speed,
    direction, gust, barometer, and the three rain accumulators); muted
    fields go out in the APRS-101 WX packet as the spec's "missing value"
    sentinel (e.g. t..., b.....) so other stations and aggregators ignore
    them.  A non-dismissable banner surfaces the active mute set on every
    page of the dashboard for the logged-in operator so the suppression
    is never forgotten.  The mute-status feed (/api/cwop/mute-status) is
    auth-gated and returns an empty list to anonymous callers, so the
    banner only appears for the operator and the public dashboard never
    leaks maintenance state.  Closes #161.  Extension to other upload
    destinations (Weather Underground, MQTT, push exports) is tracked
    separately in #162.
